# AI Reading Extension Project Rules

## Code Style and Conventions

### General

- Use TypeScript for all new code
- Maintain strict typing where possible
- Use functional components with hooks for React
- Follow consistent naming conventions

### Component Structure

- One component per file
- Use named exports
- Place related components in dedicated folders
- Use index.ts files for exporting multiple components from a folder

### State Management

- Use Zustand for global state
- Create separate slices for different feature areas
- Keep component state local when possible
- Use TypeScript interfaces for state types

### File Naming

- React components: PascalCase.tsx
- Utility functions: camelCase.ts
- Constants/types: camelCase.ts
- CSS modules: camelCase.module.css

## Development Workflow

### Chrome Extension Specific

- Remember to reload extension after code changes
- Test in multiple Chrome versions
- Check permissions carefully
- Consider both light and dark mode

### Content Script Development

- Test on various websites with different layouts
- Pay special attention to performance
- Handle error cases gracefully
- Test with different content types (articles, documentation, blogs)

### DOM Manipulation

- Use safer methods like Element.querySelector over direct DOM access
- Clean up event listeners and observers
- Avoid layout thrashing
- Be mindful of performance on large documents

## Bilingual Content Handling

### Chinese-English Text

- Use Pangu.js for proper spacing
- Consider text direction and alignment
- Test with mixed content
- Support both simplified and traditional Chinese

## UI Preferences

### Visual Style

- Follow clean, minimalist design principles
- Ensure high contrast for readability
- Use the Tailwind utility classes consistently
- Support both light and dark themes

### Accessibility

- Ensure keyboard navigation support
- Maintain sufficient color contrast
- Include proper ARIA attributes
- Test with screen readers

## Project Evolution Tracking

This section will track important project decisions and evolution as development progresses.
